# Review: TypeSafePlugin

The plugin is small and matches its spec. The connector stores a trimmed key as an AccessToken
(`typesafe.ai`) plus a Connection and rejects blank keys through `onValidate` as an `Effect.fail`.
The model resolver contributes `TypeSafeResolver` (default model `ai.typesafe.model.jev.latest`),
reads the key per call, routes through EDGE `/ai/generate/typesafe` unless overridden (moving a
connected key to `X-BYOK`), and fails a direct call with no key as an `AuthenticationError`
(`MissingKey`). Unit tests cover each piece.

Of 9 items: 7 done, 0 untested, 1 partial, 0 diverged, 1 missing. (T-2 and T-3 share T-1's fenced block, so
`deus review items` does not list them and they carry no verdict: T-2 is covered by `edge-http-client.test.ts`;
T-3 is covered by `model-resolver.test.ts` except that the space slice staying up is not asserted.) Findings:

- **No end-to-end test joins the pieces.** T-1 (paste a key, get an answer) is covered only as
  separate connector and key-resolution tests; nothing runs an operation through the contributed resolver.
- **T-2 and T-3 are not reviewable items.** They sit in T-1's fenced block, so the tool sees only T-1;
  each scenario needs its own fence.
- **QA-1 is manual** and was last run against a local proxy because the vendor blocks CORS.

